From 739fa6f3bf33c70a747aa57afaa658dbb149f3af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drew Stone <drewstone329@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:26:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(mcp): route every backend's MCP exposure through
 pluggable mount strategies

One registered strategy per CLI (opencode config layer, kimi flag, pi adapter file)
owns env, argv, cleanup, and the fail-loud decision when a CLI cannot serve the
requested servers, so adding a harness no longer edits each backend's spawn path.

Salvaged uncommitted work from 2026-07-06 against the backends as they were then.
